# Absolute minimum for local first-video.
# In the monorepo, R2 keys can also be loaded from ../server/.env.
# On a standalone droplet, put ALL secrets in this file (see .env.production.example).

NODE_ENV=development
PORT=8090
DEV_AUTH_BYPASS=1

# Production / non-bypass: project URL for ES256 JWKS verification
# SUPABASE_URL=https://mmyprzatmrfdtodsqaia.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=  # legacy HS256 only

# Phone downloads local-fallback renders from this base (same as VIDEO_ENGINE_BY_ENV.dev).
ENGINE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.35:8090

# Creators Flask API (edit-done push). Local: http://127.0.0.1:8080
# CREATOR_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# ENGINE_API_KEY=

GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Medium model for AI Template Designer (reference → EditSpec). Keep cheaper than Pro.
# GEMINI_TEMPLATE_DESIGNER_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# TEMPLATE_DESIGNER_FRAME_INTERVAL_SEC=1
# TEMPLATE_DESIGNER_MAX_FRAMES=24
PEXELS_API_KEY=
PIXABAY_API_KEY=
# WP15: KLIPY Partner Panel app key (GIF/sticker/meme overlays). Server-side bake may need KLIPY written approval.
# KLIPY_APP_KEY=
# WP52: default OFF (unrelated stickers overlapped stills). Set 1 only when deliberately testing stickers.
# KLIPY_OVERLAYS_ENABLED=1
# KLIPY_MAX_SEARCHES_PER_EDIT=8

# WP27: licensed music bed HTTPS URL for polish (empty = SFX-only). Ducking under speech is automatic.
# POLISH_MUSIC_BED_URL=

# Generated BGM (Runware ACE-Step). Off unless explicitly set. Never put a real key here.
# MUSIC_SPECIALIST=off              # off | dry | live   (legacy: =1 → dry, or live if MUSIC_SPECIALIST_LIVE=1)
# MUSIC_SPECIALIST_LIVE=0           # legacy, still honored
# MUSIC_SPECIALIST_PYTHON=          # optional explicit interpreter path
# MUSIC_SPECIALIST_TIMEOUT_MS=45000
# MUSIC_SPECIALIST_MAX_USD=0.02
# MUSIC_SPECIALIST_SFX=0
# MUSIC_BED_SOURCE=auto             # auto | licensed | generated | off
# MUSIC_DUCK_PRESET=talking         # talking (DEFAULT: bed sits 18/9/4 LU under the measured voice) | default (absolute -13/-7/-4 dB) | legacy_brief (-22/-12/-12 dB), for A/B
# MUSIC_MIX_MEASURE=0               # 1 = after a LOCAL render, render bed-only and VO-only wav stems locally and log music.mix_measured. Off by default.
# MUSIC_CARVED_TWIN=1               # default ON (voice-first: the carved bed sits further under the voice). 0 = off. Stored on each new blueprint; A/B with: npm run render-blueprint -- <bp> --carved 0|1
# MUSIC_DUCK_RELEASE_MS=300         # default 300 (lets short pauses settle); 450 was the old value. Stored on each new blueprint. A one-frame attack look-ahead (33 ms) is also stored on new blueprints
# MUSIC_MASTER_PASS=1               # default ON for local renders: two-pass ffmpeg loudnorm (I=-14, TP=-1, LRA=11) on the final MP4 audio; video is copied. 0 = off. Logs music.master_pass with before/after LUFS and true peak
# SFX_VOICE_OFFSET_LU=-10          # catalog SFX (remotion/public/sfx-library) peak this many LU under the voice's speech loudness. Never above -6. Empty catalog: no effect
# MUSIC_BED_POOL_SIZE=3            # most beds one mood pool holds. A generated bed that passed QC is appended only while the pool is under this; existing beds are never removed
# MUSIC_BED_FRESH=0                 # 1 = skip the mood pool and generate a NEW bed (paid, ~$0.0075). Default 0: reuse a pooled bed for the mood, $0
# MUSIC_BED_MOOD=                   # optional: force the pool/mood (high-energy | nostalgic | calm | tense | neutral). Default: the director's mood
# MUSIC_SPECIALIST_HARD_KILL_MS=300000  # the resolver stops waiting after MUSIC_SPECIALIST_TIMEOUT_MS; the paid child is only killed at this ceiling
# RUNWARE_API_KEY=

# WP31: polish never ships glossy-pill karaoke (plate templates -> bare karaoke type, stroke + soft shadow). Default on; 0 restores the old polish caption behaviour.
# POLISH_BARE_CAPTIONS=1

# WP33: polish plans the Metromedia VO cut grammar (1-3 word caption groups drive the cuts, ~0.85 s mean shot, hard-cut-biased transitions, a chapter card every 15-25 s). Default on; 0 restores the old polish pacing.
# POLISH_VO_CUT_GRAMMAR=1

# WP34: polish captions use the Metromedia accumulate grammar (words build up with a 4-frame blur-fade, the line hard-clears on the next cut, <= 4 words, ~7% of frame height, y 46%, sentence case). Needs POLISH_VO_CUT_GRAMMAR. Default on; 0 keeps the WP31/32 bare karaoke captions.
# POLISH_ACCUMULATE_CAPTIONS=1

# WP35: polish impact FX (overexpose flash on the hook / a major reveal, saturation glow pop on a name, 1.10 punch-in on money holds, B&W flip on emotional shots ~15% share). Needs POLISH_VO_CUT_GRAMMAR. Default on; 0 draws none.
# POLISH_IMPACT_FX=1
# WP36 faceless documentary lane (default OFF): one literal stock still per VO cut-plan shot over ~100% of the runtime; talking head hidden. Needs POLISH_VO_CUT_GRAMMAR + a stock key.
# POLISH_FACELESS_DOC=0
# WP40/42 Skill B explainer (default OFF): talking head + layouts A/B/C/D, medium pacing (hard cuts, ~3.5-4s median). Mutually exclusive with POLISH_FACELESS_DOC / POLISH_NEWSROOM_MG (faceless > newsroom > explainer). WP42 mounts into ShortVideo. Accent/ground via content-aware editPalette (lime/paper preferred, not locked).
# POLISH_EXPLAINER_SKILL=0
# WP44 Skill D newsroom MG (default OFF): B/W + signal red, GFX/CARD/HOST/EXPERT, host ~13%. Grammar newsroom-mg-grammar.yaml. Priority over Skill B when both on.
# POLISH_NEWSROOM_MG=0
# WP43 Skill C textual MG (default OFF): Jitter-class hero/emphasis type plates (elastic/trail/scramble/smear/mask/counter) over media — not karaoke. Mutes captions while a plate owns words.
# POLISH_TEXTUAL_MG=0
# WP45 Layer-2 motion-template toolkit (default OFF): sparse CLIP_01..04 moves (grid morph / slit carousel / bento camera / stacked cards) INSIDE the active polish skill, gated by that skill's allowlist. Not a new skill lane. Silent, mutes captions while on screen.
# POLISH_MOTION_TEMPLATES=0
# WP57 Kinetic-Led experimental mode (typography spine, style bible). Code default OFF. Needs POLISH_MOTION_TEMPLATES=1 to place beats.
# RECOMMENDED (=1) once the RVM person matte is provisioned on the host (RVM_PYTHON / subjectmatte/.venv-rvm + weights): with a usable matte the planner fills ~40% of the beat budget with BEHIND-the-presenter beats
# (environmental hero; word pop), spread through the edit and capped at 20 s of matted footage (45 s when RVM_DEVICE is an explicit mps / cuda). Without a matte nothing changes: face-safe headroom layouts as before.
# POLISH_KINETIC_LED=0
# Subject Stage edit style (style_id subject_stage; default OFF). The RVM speaker never moves; editing happens on stages BEHIND her (full plate / opaque card / ghost scroll / neutral accents) and once IN FRONT (S5). Polish profile + motion graphics only.
# Needs a usable RVM matte over the WHOLE run (RVM_DEVICE mps / cuda, or CPU for <= 45 s of video); otherwise the style stays off. Wins over POLISH_KINETIC_LED; off under faceless / explainer / newsroom. (Contract + Remotion shells only so far: analyze does not read it yet.)
# POLISH_SUBJECT_STAGE=0
# WP53 visual backends (default OFF; NOT new skills or toolkit ids: the backend is HOW a cutaway / counter / kinetic_text / emphasis beat is drawn). Riso = eian-riso-broll (run scripts/vendor-eian-riso.sh or set EIAN_RISO_ROOT; needs Chrome + ffmpeg to render; analyze never renders).
# POLISH_RISO_TEMPLATES=0
# EIAN_RISO_ROOT=
# Collage = gbro-collage-broll image-to-video. Analyze only stores the metaphor spec (visual_backend:collage:deferred). GEMINI_API_KEY is required ONLY when a collage job actually renders (COLLAGE_RENDER=1), never for analyze.
# POLISH_COLLAGE_BROLL=0
# COLLAGE_BROLL_ROOT=
# Anidoodle = renderer adapter only (no vendoring, music/SFX never enabled). Skipped when ANIDOODLE_ENGINE_ROOT is unset.
# POLISH_ANIDOODLE=0
# ANIDOODLE_ENGINE_ROOT=
# WP38 classic talking-head polish (neither faceless nor explainer on) uses the Skill A tools around the face: cut plan + accumulate captions + impact FX (their own flags above) + light editorial stills. This switch only moves the accumulate line to y ~58% (face-safe) and tightens the still caps (<=25% of runtime, face >=70%). Default on; 0 = pre-WP38 polish.
# POLISH_TH_SKILL_A_TOOLS=1

# Dev: force speaker cutout over B-roll (also: npm run first-video -- ... --cutout)
# FORCE_SPEAKER_CUTOUT=1
# Free multi-stage director (Stages 0/1/2/4). Off by default.
# lean (default): captions + auto-trim + auto-zoom + hook title.
# Visual toolkits stay in the repo; pass --edits= or PIPELINE_MODE=full to use them.
# PIPELINE_MODE=lean
# DIRECTOR_V2=1
# Opt-in north-star compositor (Director v2 + plate contrast + SFX). Also: --north-star
# NORTH_STAR=1
# Local acoustic/rule planner may apply delivery_shaping when --edits is omitted.
# DELIVERY_SHAPING_AUTO=1
# Optional transcript-only LLM emphasis proposals (default off).
# DELIVERY_LLM_EMPHASIS=0

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Template-driven edit (OpenRouter Video API)
OPENROUTER_SEEDANCE_MODEL=bytedance/seedance-2.0-mini

# --- Motion-graphics worker (Claude) -------------------------------------
# Writes procedural Remotion graphics from Director briefs (server/src/motionWorker).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Model (default claude-sonnet-5-5) and effort (default: the model's own default).
MOTION_WORKER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
MOTION_WORKER_EFFORT=
# Native Anthropic prompt caching of the stable system prompt (default on; 0 = off, for baselines).
MOTION_WORKER_PROMPT_CACHE=

# R2 — required on standalone droplet (optional locally if ../server/.env exists)
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET_NAME=
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Optional. Leave blank — first videos render on this Mac, then upload to R2.
# Fill after docs/remotion-lambda-deploy.md (function + site deploy).
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
REMOTION_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
REMOTION_FUNCTION_NAME=
REMOTION_SERVE_URL=
REMOTION_COMPOSITION_ID=ShortVideo
REMOTION_FRAMES_PER_LAMBDA=120
# REMOTION_S3_OUTPUT_BUCKET=

# --- WP1: product editing profile and per-edit Claude bound (all optional; unset = today's behaviour) ---
# PRODUCT_EDIT_PROFILE=mvp        # explicit opt-out to the mvp profile (only the exact string "mvp"; case-sensitive, surrounding spaces are trimmed): whole-video Director, opening plan, creator-B-roll-only, legibility rules. Not the default. Not settable by API callers.
# PRODUCT_EDIT_PROFILE=legacy     # explicit opt-out to the pre-WP1 behaviour (only the exact string "legacy"; its cache keys are the old ones). Not the default.
# PRODUCT_EDIT_PROFILE=cuts       # THE DEFAULT (since WP7C): cuts-first. Unset, empty or any unrecognized value (a typo) resolves to cuts and logs a warning. Silence + filler trim, transcript retake/restart/self-correction trim and background-noise reduction; skips the visual Director, B-roll, generated and motion graphics, and delivery shaping. Set PRODUCT_EDIT_PROFILE=legacy or mvp only to opt out.
# PRODUCT_EDIT_PROFILE=polish     # opt-in (WP8A, the exact string "polish"): Stage A = everything the cuts profile does to the speech (denoise, AI keep-plan, fluency scrub, retakes, forced trim), THEN Stage B = the mvp visual editor (Director, toolkits, captions); generated graphics stay off unless MOTION_GRAPHICS_ENABLED is on. Not the default; cuts stays the default.
# CUTS_DENOISE_ENABLED=true       # cuts profile only: reduce background noise on the talking-head audio (afftdn). false cuts without denoising. A failed denoise warns (cuts_denoise_failed) and keeps the original audio.
# CUTS_DENOISE_NR_DB=12           # cuts profile only: noise reduction in dB (clamped 4-30). Gentle by default; high values make speech sound watery.
# CUTS_DENOISE_HIGHPASS_HZ=80     # cuts profile only: high-pass cutoff in Hz for rumble and hum (clamped 40-200).
# CLAUDE_EDIT_BUDGET_USD=         # hard per-edit cap on estimated Claude spend (dollars). No default on purpose. With the mvp profile and MOTION_GRAPHICS_ENABLED=true, unset/0 switches generated graphics OFF and the job records claude_graphics_disabled:claude_budget_unconfigured (a negative value also switches them off: ...:claude_budget_invalid).
# CLAUDE_EDIT_MAX_REQUESTS=       # optional; default = graphics cap x (1 + repair attempts)
# CLAUDE_EDIT_MAX_TOKENS=         # optional per-call output ceiling (>= 4000, default 12000)

# --- WP2: URL ingest safety ---
# INGEST_ALLOWED_PRIVATE_HOSTS=   # default empty: loopback, link-local, private and cloud-metadata addresses are always refused. Exact hostnames only, comma separated.

# --- WP3C: per-edit Gemini request cap (optional; unset = today's behaviour) ---
# GEMINI_EDIT_MAX_REQUESTS=       # max Gemini HTTP attempts in ONE analyze job, retries included. At the cap no further request is sent; stages use their fallbacks and the job finishes.
#                                 # UNSET OR 0 MEANS NO CAP (Gemini attempts are unbounded). On PRODUCT_EDIT_PROFILE=mvp the job then records the warning gemini_edit_budget_unconfigured;
#                                 # it is only a warning (the job is NOT refused). Set a positive request count before any paid run. A negative value fails closed (no Gemini request at all); a non-numeric value is read as unset (0 = no cap), so check the number.

# --- polish production trial (all optional and commented; unset = today's default, cuts; the HTTP analyze path and first-video read the SAME variables) ---
# PRODUCT_EDIT_PROFILE=polish     # (see the polish line above) the HTTP product path then runs the same stack as first-video: speech cuts, then the Edit Look Director.
# POLISH_DEFAULT_EDITS=lean       # polish only: what is edited when the request / CLI names no edits. lean (default) = captions + zoom + hook title, kinetic text, lockup, card, bubble, emphasis, counter (no stock B-roll search); all = every toolkit (creator B-roll stays user-only).
# MOTION_GRAPHICS_ENABLED=1       # polish: with no Claude bound the motion stage runs LIBRARY-ONLY (ready-made compositions, no Claude call, job graphics status "library_only"); unset/0 = no generated graphics.
# GEMINI_EDIT_MAX_REQUESTS=8      # per-edit Gemini attempt cap; polish reserves slots for the keep-plan, Director v2 and the motion Director (occupancy gets one attempt). Below 4 starves the motion Director.
# CLAUDE_EDIT_BUDGET_USD=         # needed ONLY if you want Claude to build graphics the library cannot (then also set a request cap). Library-only polish needs no Claude key.
